Z||000003||JSocha||05-01-2001||11:21 AM||||Sounds like your town needs money!  Good luck at the hearing as typically the Judge upholds the ticket irregardless of what evidence you have.<P>I got to pay somebody elses ticket last November cause I was the last vehicle in a group of 4 and the HP couldn't get out to get the one he clocked.<P>I contested it, the officer didn't have to prove a thing and I had evidence to back my position and the Judge said he believed the officer and the reading of the Laser (even though it was the officers word what the Laser said).  <P>Tried to appeal it but the appeal court wouldn't hear my case even though I informed them that I could now show even more evidence based on the testimony of the officer at the first hearing that didn't calculate out when I gave our engineer the figures who did some calculations.<P><B>Today's Thought:</B><BR>Our socity today talks about scams, telephone, mail, door-to-door, etc., and frowns upon them and will do anything to convict and stop the perpatrators to these scams and ripping off the public.<P>Yet, IMO, government employees such as police and HP officers have the biggest scam going to collect money and rip off the public.  <P>You can be 100% innocent of a traffic violation, contest it with all the evidence, testimony and witnesses in the world and the judge of that court and town/city will naturally uphold any violation issued by the officer based on his testimony and what he wrote down even if it is false and a lie.<P>Now is that a scam or not!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
