Z||000011||thomas_l||05-01-2001||01:29 PM||||The cop was just being a dick. I probably could've rode by in my silver (well more gray) 87 GT with its even louder rusty old stock muffler and tips, speeding in 3rd gear, radio turned up, and throwing things at the cop and he wouldn't even look. Finally getting my hair cut and looking like the law abiding grown-up has reduced the cop attention I get. <P>Funny story - My wife's son got pulled over twice in his freshly painted (lt met blue) 87 Caprice ex-police car in Alpharetta: First time he got a seat belt ticket (cop pulled along side at a red light - DOH!) and second time was just after dusk and his tag light was burned out. Yes that GD little lamp over the licence plate. The stupid part is that his Mom works for the city, the car was bought at a city auction, and all the cops know both the car and the kid driving it and his mom. Talk about harassment!! They just saw a young guy sporting a nice car (he cruises - not a speeder) and figured he was probably good for an open container or roaches in his ashtray. Too bad they don't have enough free time arrest some real threats to society sometimes.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fearlessdata.com/fiero/87GT_small.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000012||rogergarrison||05-01-2001||01:30 PM||||If you do beat it, same cop will be even more on the lookout to get you for anything, like a burned out licence plate lite. I always get nervous passing a cop, even if im doing everything within the law. If ones behind me, i pull into anything, gas sta, car wash to let him pass me. Mine looks like a Ferrari, sounds like one, red, so I know there gunning for me. No the gray hair dont help. I know a couple times ive gotten ticket just so the cop could brag to their buds about stopping a Ferrari. I paid one speeding ticket,$80 for 5 over limit of 55. I went to bank before I went to pay it, and bought $80 worth of pennies. Took the police chief and 2 counter people almost 2 hours to count. My lawyer said they had to accept it because it us government legal currency. I still had to pay, but got some satisfaction watching them cuss me out to themselves. Ive been thru same town again several times and they ignore me now, lol.<P>BTW...did you get written permission from Hiway Patrol to make a facimile of thier ticket???? LMAO<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||1FST2M6||05-01-2001||02:02 PM||||this is tha actuall part of the law he's tryin to get me with... <P>(c) It shall be unlawful for any person to sell or offer for sale<BR>  any muffler which causes excessive or unusual noise or annoying<BR>  smoke or any muffler cutout, bypass, or similar device for use on a<BR>  motor vehicle or for any person to use, to sell, or to offer for<BR>  sale any motor vehicle equipped with any such muffler, muffler<BR>  cutout, bypass, or similar device. Any person violating this<BR>  subsection shall be guilty of a misdemeanor.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||JSocha||05-01-2001||02:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>(c) It shall be unlawful for any person to sell or offer for sale<BR>  any muffler which causes excessive or unusual noise or annoying<BR>  smoke or any muffler cutout, bypass, or similar device for use on a<BR>  motor vehicle or for any person to use, to sell, or to offer for<BR>  sale any motor vehicle equipped with any such muffler, muffler<BR>  cutout, bypass, or similar device. Any person violating this<BR>  subsection shall be guilty of a misdemeanor.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well then, it's setlled, I'm interested in your system if your <I>"selling"</I> since obviously he thinks you were "advertising"!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
