Z||000016||sameul||05-01-2001||03:45 PM||||Two things-  one cops really do like to pull over red cars (I used to think maybe people in red cars drove faster).  I used to drive a beat up 85 white ford ranger with a ladder rack like a bat out of hell(if I was on the freeway I was doing at least 85).  I think I must have been pulled over about 7 times and never got a ticket.  I have, however, received two tickets for speeding once in my brothers RED 88 acura legend and once in my girlfriends RED honda del sol.  The really interesting thing is that I was only pulled over a total of twice and that I RARELY drove their cars.  So think twice before you put on that shiny new coat of paint (maybe go for radar absorbing carbon fiber ala stealth fighter!).<BR>  Second there is an organization called the National Motorist Association (of which I am a member) that will reimburse you for the cost of a speeding ticket if you fight it in court (and have been a member for at least a month I think).  These are the same folks who got the max speed limit back up to 65.  Their website is <A HREF="http://www.motorist.org." TARGET=_blank>www.motorist.org.</A> ||||reg||8
Z||000017||Shaun41178||05-01-2001||04:20 PM||||I know that in Califonia it states that the car has to be a certain DB level at idle from a certain distance away.  Now the only way the guy can bust you and do it legally is if has a meter there to read how many decibels it is making.  The EPA set this standard so it might be for all states in the US.  If this is the case then he can't give a ticket for loud exhaust cause he has no idea if it is over the given Db level unless he has a meter there with him.  Also your car can be as loud as you want when accelerating.  It just has to be a certain Db when idleing.<P>Georgia might have it written differently in their books however.<P>I got pulled over for speeding 4 years ago right after I got my Fiero.  I left the car running so he writes me a ticket for speeding and the gives me a warning for loud exhaust.  I was like WTF!  I still have the stock exhaust on it from the factory and he said it was too loud.  If that was the case then the guy should be sitting next to car dealerships waiting for cars to pull out and then hit them with loud exhaust tickets.<P>Unless they have a meter there to prove how loud it is then that ticket is bogus.<P>Good luck in fighting it.  I know you will win.  Cop won't care if you do though.  He gets payed time and a half for being in court.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000018||thomas_l||05-01-2001||04:21 PM||||my licence plate lamps & seat belts work well  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000019||Black88GT||05-01-2001||04:21 PM||||Yeah I agree with JSocha  about how cops can speed and such and get away with it.  One time with my Dad, a cop was in front of us going 10 over the limit.  My Dad kept up with him for a few miles, about 10 car lengths behind, and the cop slammed on his brakes and told us to pull over only to *****  about how we were speeding.<P>The thing I don't understand about the "noise pollution" laws, is why they don't apply to motorcycles specifically Harley's.  While there are a bunch of ricers around here with fart can exhausts, atleast they don't come chugging down my block at 3 AM (when the bar closes) and wake the dead.  Laws are laws but they should be for everyone.<P>FIGHT THE POWER<P><p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||stimpy||05-01-2001||04:47 PM||||That is an unbelieveably subjectively written law. Remind me never to drive in Georgia. No doubt my Flowmaster would cause fits. I bet if I were to drive my dads bright red 86 GT with the supercharged 3.8 (no muffler, just Ansa tips) I'd get locked up!<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||1FST2M6||05-01-2001||04:49 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.greddy.com/CHPnoisepolicies.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.greddy.com/CHPnoisepolicies.html</A> <P>California is know through out the performance market for having the strictest noise ordanances in the US and i EASILY pass thier guidlines... I'm really suprised i never got nailed in the se with no cat and free-er flowing exhaust. it was WAY louder than what i have now! ||||reg||1
Z||000022||Indiana_resto_guy||05-01-2001||05:07 PM||||Don't you know ANY policemen (or women) to take to court with you who will state that in his/her opinion your car is not loud?<BR>Espically @ 4:30 in the afternoon? (I'm sure that disturbing the peace can't be used in this one!)<BR>Get better documentation besides just a 'sticker'!<BR>You might get in contact with the MFG. of your system and request their paperwork.<BR>(just a thought)||||reg||1
Z||000023||Slammed Fiero||05-01-2001||05:34 PM||||I have had friends with imports in the same situation. Greddy faxed them a letter saying it was legal and the specs of the muffler.<P>I had a cop follow me home one night , from in town to my house in the burbs (15 min away) he heard me downshift (no cat) and decided to see what was up , no ticket , he said just watch myself around town with the loud crackling downshifts<P><BR>JM||||reg||1
Z||000024||fieroparts.com||05-01-2001||05:49 PM||||Was it a Borla?||||reg||14
Z||000025||JSocha||05-01-2001||05:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Yeah I agree with JSocha  about how cops can speed and such and get away with it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I didn't say he was speeding  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">.  He was sitting off on the side, my radar detector going off like crazy for about 5 to 6 miles, suddenly everyone (4 vehicles in front of me) were braking like mad, radar detector went off like there was no tomorrow and then the very first vehicles headlights lit up the side emblem of the HP.<P>I went from 65 MPH down to 45MPH just to avoid hitting the car right in front of me and then speeded back up to 60MPH.<P>When the first vehicle was closer to where the HP was sitting, the HP put on his headlights, moved forward a bit and then put on his cherry's (Christmas time in November) and then tried to pull out again, but the three vehicles behind the first vehicle in our group (plus mine) would not move over into the other lane to let him out because we were to close by then.<P>Finally, he pulled out after me, followed me for over a mile and a half and since he didn't pull out in the passing lane (like it looked like he was going to when he pulled out after me and the vehicle in front of me now doing 60 MPH since everyone started braking in a 65 MPH zone), I slowed down to pull over so he could pass and he pulled over with me cause it did not look like he was going to pass me.<P>When he told me he clocked me doing 76MPH in a 65MPH zone, it shocked me so much I told him he had the wrong guy as I pointed down the road.<P>We had been doing between 65 and 67.5 MPH that whole evening.  I knew when I left town to the time we got picked up and our engineer here at the shop calculated my speed average at between 55 and 63 MPH to cover the distance I did that evening.  Our engineer even calculated the rate based on the time I arrived in respective towns on the way with the milage to each town.  All were under 65MPH and accounted for slowdowns or difference in speed.<P>This was after the first hearing.<P>At court, the officer testified that he clocked me at 76MPH at 906.3 ft (Laser gun reading) and tracked me for 45 seconds before pulling out behind me from where he was sitting.<P>Our engineer, after I lost the first hearing and was working on an appeal, based on the testimony of the officer calculated that I would have had to be driving 13.73 MPH to cover 906.3' in 45 seconds.<P>In addition, since I drove 1 1/2 miles from the time he pulled out to the time I finally pulled over, we gave him the benefit of the doubt that this was the total time from the time he clocked me to the time I was pulled over.  <P>So we said 10 seconds from the time of his reading to where he was positioned when I may have passed with the remaining 35 seconds going toward the 1 1/2 miles that I covered before I electively slowed down and pulled over to get out of his way.<P>10 Seconds at 906.3' = 61.79MPH (right around the 60 MPH I and the vehicle in front of me were now doing after the braking and before we knew where or if there was an HP).<P>35 seconds at a distance of 1 1/2 miles = 154.29 MPH to cover that distance in that time in a 2001 Dodge 1-ton!  Stock  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Our engineer calculated it out at 76 MPH for 906.3', I should have covered that distance in 8.11 seconds not 45 seconds like the officer testified.<P>The appeals court would not hear my case even though my attorney assited me in submitting that there was new evidence that I could show that I did not commit this violation and that I could prove and refute the officer's testimony.<P>Nope...Appeals court wasn't interested and was going by the first ruling and would stand behind it.<P>I know there is an officer (or perhaps more) on this post, one who "locks up the bad guys...click" &lt;on a thread I started...What not to say to a police officer&gt;, but I lost all respect for HP officers after that incident and the court system in general.<P>Guilty...never to be proven innocent.<P>Now, I'm fighting another legal battle regarding my property and "easement" rights just so a power company can put high power lines across my property and devalue it at the same time.<P>Sorry if it seems like I am venting.  Lately, public officials are really getting to me and plucking the last nerve I have left!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||rogergarrison||05-01-2001||08:12 PM||||<BR>Don't you know ANY policemen (or women) to take to court with you who will state that in his/her opinion your car is not loud?<P>FAT CHANCE OF THAT EVER HAPPENING !!!!!!! I have no respect for any police anymore. They all seem to have a 'macho' mentality. Sorry if any policemen are here, but thats how I feel. If I need one, they oblige only if its convenient to them. I try to shut up cars next door to me at all hours with boom radios turned up all the time, even call them. What do they do, threaten to cite me for creating a disturbance...whats with that? Screw the cops, Ill drive how I damn well please anymore, if I get caught, Ill just pay the fine and mark it up as a necessary expense. Whatr they gonna do, take my licence, theres already a million people driving without one. There not gonna hurt my insurance anymore, Im self insured. Ill get off my soap box now, sorry to babble so long, but cops now just piss me off.||||reg||1
Z||000027||grinthock||05-01-2001||08:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>If you do beat it, same cop will be even more on the lookout to get you for anything, like a burned out licence plate lite. I always get nervous passing a cop, even if im doing everything within the law. If ones behind me, i pull into anything, gas sta, car wash to let him pass me. Mine looks like a Ferrari, sounds like one, red, so I know there gunning for me. No the gray hair dont help. I know a couple times ive gotten ticket just so the cop could brag to their buds about stopping a Ferrari. I paid one speeding ticket,$80 for 5 over limit of 55. I went to bank before I went to pay it, and bought $80 worth of pennies. Took the police chief and 2 counter people almost 2 hours to count. My lawyer said they had to accept it because it us government legal currency. I still had to pay, but got some satisfaction watching them cuss me out to themselves. Ive been thru same town again several times and they ignore me now, lol.<P>BTW...did you get written permission from Hiway Patrol to make a facimile of thier ticket???? LMAO<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good way to piss them off, here in Canada, anything over 100 of the same denomination we are not required to accept as legal tender.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000028||FieroLisa||05-01-2001||08:55 PM||||so now wouldn't be a good time for me to tell you guys that I've gotten out of..ummm 4 tickets in court now?  Let's see, a speeding (81 in 65), an accident where I rear-ended an explorer, and a couple window tint ones. But no moving violations for me, just a bunch of "headlight violations" Every one of those I was written a ticket, took it to court, and they were just too busy to hear my cases, so they made me pay a $40 court fee and that's it.  Good stuff.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT- 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air,<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000029||JSocha||05-01-2001||09:18 PM||||FieroLisa?   Want to be my Lawyer?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I've been able to talk myself out of many speeding tickets in the past and have only got warnings (haven't sped in over a year...wife can testify to that...mellowing out in my young age...egad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">...).<P>Just about got one in Bismarck after visiting with RossT on Friday night.  <P>Couldn't see the road as it started raining and was dark.  Turned on the windshield wipers, instant smear and could not see the lines on the road (they really need to paint them here in ND) or the road itself and ended up crossing over into the oncoming lane.  Lucky me, there was a police officer coming the other way who graciously let me know it.<P>Pulled into the motels parking lot and got out cause I didn't have my seatbelt on and was getting my licence out.  <P>Got yelled at to get back in the vehicle...but didn't and the officer was nice enough not to give me a $40 ticket in the end for being in the wrong lane due to the circumstances I am assuming or my cooperation.<P>In the meantime, grocieries are in the back box of the truck and my friend Doug is hugging the three bottles of alcohol we just picked up and decided to keep in the cab with us of the truck saying "Officer can't have!  Officer can't have!  No! No! Mine!" (loud enough for the neighbors to hear) while the officer is coming with the ticket up to my door.<P>Been pulled over for tinted windows also. Typically just paid the fine and let them enjoy their Christmas Party at the end of the year.  I always tell the HP that after being issued a $20 ticket for tinted windows that I get, "Enjoy your Christmas Party this year as it is on me".  Lack of humor is all I can say.<P>Been pulled over for no reason at all...oh...except for a (what I will call surprise) vehicle inspection...yeah right officer, whatever!  Do I have "STUPID" plastered across my forehead?<P>You want to look in my trunk?  Do you have probable cause for pulling me over or a search warrent?  <P>Oh!  Probable Cause you say? Don't think so as you just told me the reason why you pulled me over is that you are performing random vehicle inspections today for lights, brakes, signals, etc.!<P>Again, I reiterate..."Do I have 'STUPID' plastered across my forehead?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000030||KRMFiero||05-01-2001||09:33 PM||||That sucks dude    <P>::listing to my friends Jeep with a cherry bomb and no cat::   maybe i should warn him? its shaking my house at idle||||reg||1
Z||000031||Sleeper||05-01-2001||11:56 PM||||your a target because of the color of your car. its the same with me.<P>i got a loud exhaust ticket last month but it was only $70 not $219. the PO-PO told me my exhaust was "too loud for the community" and "they don't make fieros like this". its stock exhaust except for the tips(pace setter) but the PO-lice just like to pick on ppl with nice cars nowdays. <P>the streetraces are a field-day for the PO-PO, they love giving outrageous ticket like this one.||||reg||1
Z||000032||Nashco||05-02-2001||12:43 AM||||Well, just thougth I'd clear something up for you Black88GT.  I work at a testing facility for Harley-Davidson, and there is most definitely noise pollution laws that apply to Harley-Davidsons just like Pontiacs and Peugots.  We tune them from the factory to meet all the requirements.  If somebody tweaks them after they buy them, they are still required to conform to the laws.  Just because they don't get busted doesn't mean they don't have laws that apply to them.  I work with some great guys and gals who ride H-Ds, and hate to hear stereotypes made.  Just like the stereotypes about people who drive orange cars with a loud exhaust!<P>Oh, and for the record, I have very little respect for cops.  To add to to my feelings, I got my first ticket the other day for (long story short) the cop not liking my driving habits.  I didn't do anything illegal, but he found some bullcrap to write a ticket for.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000033||Spektyr||05-02-2001||04:40 AM||||I have a fun little story...<P>Several years ago when I was in the Navy and stationed in Florida I had a nice RED Nissan pickup that was... well modified to earn gas money.  (20 dollar pick up races at a light, one every 2 weeks or so and I never had to buy gas).<P>Well, me and a buddy ran off base to make a beer run, me driving my hotrod Nissan.  Now I'm the only one who's 21, and the beer is for a bunch of under 21 folks.  (I say if you're old enough to fight and die for your country, you can drink a damn beer, but that's a different arguement.)  I pull up at a light and there's a cop car about 4 cars behind me, but I don't think anything of it because I'm driving responsibly.<P>The light turns green and I pull away, making the tiniest little squeal as my back tire has trouble gaining a foothold on the light sand at the intersection.  I didn't run it in 1st gear, I shifted early and in no way accelerated at anything close to what the truck could do.  (and it wasn't all THAT fast anyway).<P>Sure enough, Mr Macho pulls me over.  He claims that I was showing off for my buddy, to which I nicely state, "Sir, if I was going to show off, I'd have gone faster, and I'd have done it on the flightline on base where there isn't a speed limit."  Of course he doesn't like this and gets even snootier when I hand him my military ID and Drivers License.  He throws my Military ID back into the truck claiming I'm trying to get some sort of special treatment.  I quoted the Uniform Code of Military Justice which states that as an Active Duty serviceman I must identify myself as such to all police I come in contact with.  Now he's really ticked because he's being an ******* , I'm being nice and it's making him look bad.<P>So he writes me a ticket for "Racing on the Highway", to which I comment that I didn't think that street was a highway.  He replies, "What did you think it was?".  I say, "A street."  He gives me a dirty look and walks away.<P>The JAG Corps lawyer I knew said to just pay the ticket so I did.  Florida is a really messed up state.  Be careful driving down there as the local police have the reputation of ticketing EVERYONE they can, including other police officers!<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000034||Raydar||05-02-2001||10:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektyr:<BR><B>...Be careful driving down there as the local police have the reputation of ticketing EVERYONE they can, including other police officers!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> <P>What?! No "professional courtesy"?! <BR>What in the hell is this country coming to?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000035||firstfiero||05-02-2001||10:32 AM||||    Here's a good one. This happened befor the fiero when I had an 80 bmw 528i. I was a big bimmer nut back then. anyway  One night about 1:00 in the morning I was going home from work when I see a cop coming twoards me. I look in my mirror after he goes by and see him turn around in a parking lot and come back flying twoard me. He gets right on my ass and follows me a few miles. Finnal he pops the lights on and pulls me over. Now I'm totally miffed because I know I wasn't speeding. When he comes up to the car and I ask him what the problem is he tells me that he has to see my license plate from at least 50 ft away and because one of my 2 license plate lights was burned out he couldn't see me from any farther then 40. Gave me a card to have filled out when I got it fixed. I wanted to tell him I knew why he pulled me over because he was hoping for the big pay off a DUI. I was coming home from work so he didn't get lucky. You don't even want to get me  started on how unconstitusional dui checks are! <P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif"> <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||14
Z||000036||Predator||05-02-2001||11:15 AM||||That really sucks man. Now you got me worried. I'm a little on the loud side myself. There are Coffee can cars running around all over Roswell a lot louder than you or I. Heck there is a girl in a white Geo that has a Stereo so loud that it literally rocks my house when she drives by. Sounds like a bored cop looking for someone to bust. My Torino was twice as loud as your car, and I never got pulled over for it. One thing funny I saw was a 300 ZX with dual Coffee cans hanging off the back. They were so big they almost took up the whole backend. Talk about stupid looking, and I can guarantee those were loud. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Predator (edited 05-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000037||fierohoho||05-02-2001||10:45 PM||||Just remember, when a cop goes to court, if it's his day off, he's getting time and a half for probably a 2 hour minimum even if your trial takes 10 minutes. Win or loose he's happy either way and your there for free.||||reg||1
Z||000038||Black88GT||05-02-2001||10:55 PM||||I wasn't "stereotyping" Harley owners.  There isn't one Harley in this entire state that is even remotely close to being as quiet as 95% of the cars on the road. I have personally been next to over 30 Harleys before and just for the hell of it I revved my car up to about 5000 RPMs to see if I could hear it, and I couldn't even tell the car was up that high all I could hear was the Harley.  <P>I don't really have that big of a problem with them during the day, I could care less I actually think some of them are nice and loud in a classy way.  However after I worked a 16 hour day and I have to wake up and do it all over, I don't appreciate a group of Harley owners breaking the sound barrier at 3 in the morning...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000039||rogergarrison||05-02-2001||11:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B> Good way to piss them off, here in Canada, anything over 100 of the same denomination we are not required to accept as legal tender.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>mmmmmmmm, OK, go with 100 pennies, 100 nickles, 100 dimes yadayadayada man that would really have em confused, lol. Maybe a whole bundle of totally crinkled up bills, take em a while to smooth out so they could count em. Id do anything to be a total pain in the butt, just to tick em off. After they count it all, ask for parking validation too. lmao.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000040||fierospeeder||05-03-2001||01:42 AM||||I know how all of you guys feel.<P>Got two tickets within a 6 month period, and got pulled over 3 times in the 6 month period.<P>My girlfriend and i are in the car and theres a red light, im looking at the light on top thats overhead, and i look both ways and take my right turn.  theres cars in front of us because theres another light.  So behind us comes a SUV Cop, gas guzler.  So he comes up, wondering what the hell i did, and says i took a right turn on red.  I told him i didn't see it and gives me a ticket.  the passenger cop is on my passenger side checking my g/f out wondering what the fu.  After the ticket i approach the red light.  The cop is still in his SUV and hes about 300 ft behind me.  Suddenly a car goes through the red light.  My g/f and i are shocked that, that guy didn't get pulled over.  And going through a light is 100% worse then what i did, looking both ways and turning.   going through reds is deadly.<P>going through yellow is illegal, learned that in traffic school, and you have the right in illinois to look at the cops gun when he pulls you over.<P>2nd story, im coming home from school and im driving normally in my tbird turbo.  And i see lights behind me, wondering what the its always me.  I pull on the side, and says i have no front license plate.  Illinois law, must have front plate.  He gives me a verbal warning and lets me go.  I did point out to him, how do i put the plate in the front cause its pointy.  He said go to the dealership.   I have to bend the plate almost 45 degrees if i want it to be on the front bumper.  The factory had a plate holder, im lucky to find one at the junkyard, its like trying to find an indy fiero.<P>3rd.  Recently.  Im driving to school, and i blame my g/f for making me drop her kid at daycare so i have to take another road.  So im going 10 over, and theres a car in front of me, he gets in the right lane.  My car speeds up going down the hills.  I look in my mirror and cop lights, im like Yup, i got a ticket for something.  So i get in the left turn lane and take a left turn, and i see him in the mirror telling me to get in the parking lot.  He asks what was i doing, i said no idea.  He says how fast was i going, said no idea, he said clocked me at 53, asked if i knew the speedlimit,  I WAS FICKING honest and said 35.  I said i was going over the hill and probably went to fast.  He says well i got you on the flat road.  He also says, next time an emergency vehicle is on the road, pull to the right, i said uh there was cars on the right so i couldn't.  "real reason, uh i knew i was getting pulled over"<BR>The cops says i have 15 days to pay for the ticket, My ass.<P>I read the book that he gave me, stating you have 7 business days to pay.  I go to the courthouse to pay it.  I get my receipt, <BR>the ticket costs 75 bucks.<BR>but really it costs<BR>clerk's fees  10<BR>court automation fee 5<BR>court fund fee 5<BR>surcharge fund 8<BR>leads maintenance fund 2<BR>trauma center fee 5<BR>fine amount 40    owe thats how much it is<BR>total assesment   75.00 american dollars<BR>first time i learned its really 40 but im paying for some bull@(%%<BR>So i paid it the last day of the 7 business days<BR>The next day i get a letter says i have to appear in court because i didn't pay.  I guess the cop is really smart saying i got 15.  I called up and found out court is canceled.  load of crap.<P>I have lost respect for 90% of cops.  I would love to be in a position higher then a cop to say, fu(( off, like an FBI agent, military officer, etc... uh a lawyer.<P>You just have to mess up just once in 10 second period to get a ticket.  While you drive the speed limit for an hour, watching jack a$$ speeding road rage, no turn signals running red lights, tailgating, and YOUR THE BAD GUY.    Really Sucks.<P>Someone has to invent a camera that records the speed or use the kind that cops have, so there is proof that we didn't do anything.  <BR>Unless we can be watching the speedometer 100% of the time and just be wrong in court.<P>totally sucks.  oh in illinois, some guy dropped his cellular phone and some really famous MODEL "FAMOUS" got hurt, liver damage and something else.  While driving and her car ran into a pole.  So now they are gonna try to make it illegal to use cellular phones, while cops are saying they got better things to do then pull people over for that.||||reg||1
Z||000041||AusFiero||05-03-2001||10:17 AM||||The EPA (Eviromental Protection Authority) here in Australia set up roadside testing stations to randomly check noise levels of cars and trucks, with police assistance. Usually where lots of hot cars hangout I might add.<P>Fines for illegal exhaust systems putting out too many decibels start at $2000 and a defect sticker on the vehicle. Which means it is off the road basically. <P>But now the real clincher. Once you have fixed the "illegal" exhaust system you then have to pay the EPA $2000 more to retest your car and give you a certificate to be able to re-register your car.<P>Oh...and forget court appeals. Courts figure the EPA equipment is gosphel basically and won't even hear an appeal. <P>Put Up..Shut Up...Pay Up is about the best you would get.||||reg||8
